  "The file ds.csv has variables of unknown types: 'y' (reel), 'z' (foo) and 'w' (foo); a CSV file only stores real and integer variables. The file ds.csv has variables whose rows have different types: 'u' (real and integer) and 'w' (integer and foo); the rows of a variable must have the same type. The file ds.csv has a variable that is neither real nor integer: 't' (discrete); only an HDF file can store it."
# ---
# name: test_from_csv_refuses_invalid_variable_types[mixed]
  "The file ds.csv has a variable whose rows have different types: 'y' (real and discrete); the rows of a variable must have the same type."
# ---
# name: test_from_csv_refuses_invalid_variable_types[several-unsupported]
  "The file ds.csv has variables that are neither real nor integer: 't' (discrete), 'm' (catalog) and 'c' (categorical); only an HDF file can store them."
# ---
# name: test_from_csv_refuses_invalid_variable_types[unknown]
  "The file ds.csv has a variable of unknown type: 'y' (reel); a CSV file only stores real and integer variables."
# ---
# name: test_from_csv_with_a_header_longer_than_the_rows
  "The file ds.csv has 1 column but the header has 3 fields: 'name', 'lower_bound' and 'upper_bound'."
# ---
